# Shared inputs and output contract (all critics)
You are ONE of three independent critics evaluating a launch film for **Agentic Office** (an AI workspace that edits the real Word/Excel/PowerPoint files inside a folder together and lets the user review and accept or reject every change). The other critics judge other things; stay strictly in your lane.

Inputs, in the working directory:
- ../WHAT_WE_WANT.md: marketing brief, audience, rules, success test.
- ../context/Agentic_Office_Strategy/strategy/07_PERSONAS.md: the target customer (Maya, an associate in fund finance; David, the CFO).
- ../RESEARCH_PAIN.md: real public complaints (evidence of the customer's pain).
- ../UI_REUSE.md: the real product footage that exists, and what must never be shown (the source of product truth and approved claims).
- The CANDIDATE named in the task (a script, and in stage 2 also rendered frames with timestamps and a timeline).

Product truth / approved claims: the app edits the native model, memo and deck in one workspace; it shows proposed changes (tracked changes, per-cell bars, a Changes panel with per-file groups); the user accepts or rejects; the demo task is DACH Q4 8.9 → 8.5 with the memo going from €71–73m to €74.6m and 10 of 10 changes accepted. NOT approved: time savings, speed benchmarks, privacy guarantees, "never wrong", fully autonomous sending, a recorded Reject result (not captured yet), the internal name "Hermes", real AI brand logos.

Return ONLY a JSON object (no prose before or after) with this schema:
{
 "critic": "<craft|story|customer_psychology>",
 "stage": "<script|animatic>",
 "score": 0-100,
 "dimension_scores": {"<dimension>": 0-100, ...},
 "issues": [{"shot_id": "beat N or mm:ss", "category": "<snake_case>", "severity": 0.0-1.0, "confidence": 0.0-1.0, "evidence": "<what you saw, quote the script or frame>", "suggested_action": "<a concrete change to that beat>"}],
 "constraint_failures": [{"rule": "<which hard rule>", "shot_id": "...", "evidence": "..."}],
 "revision_scope": "<none|single_shot|shot_sequence|opening|product_demo|ending|whole>",
 "top_revision": "<the single highest-impact change, in one sentence>"
}
Rules: every issue needs evidence and a concrete action. "Make it better" is not allowed. Judge only what a viewer would actually see and hear, not what the writer intended. List at most 8 issues, highest severity first. Low confidence means "verify", not "regenerate".
# What we want: the Agentic Office launch film (v4 brief)

*Written 2026-10-12, after v3 was rejected: "I can't understand where AI is causing the problem. The workflow is not shown."*

## 1. Why v1–v3 didn't work
- They showed **a stressed person**, not **the workflow** that stresses her.
- "AI fails" was **abstract**: red marks, a cheerful man in orange. Nobody could say *what the AI did wrong*.
- Messages flashed by too fast to read, so the story lived in text nobody saw.
- The real pain from our deck never appeared: **AI answers in a chat, while the work sits in folders, so the human carries everything across.**

## 2. The one insight the film must land
> **Today, you drive and the AI suggests.**
> You upload the files, explain the context, copy the answer, paste it into Word, fix the formatting, update the model by hand, rebuild the deck the chatbot "made", and check everything yourself.
>
> **With Agentic Office it's reversed: the AI drives and you approve.**
> It works *inside* your folder (model, memo and deck together), shows every change, and you accept or reject.

Everything in the film either shows the human doing the AI's job, or shows the AI doing the job while the human approves.

## 3. Source of truth (our own material)
| Source | What it gives the film |
|---|---|
| Deck slide 1: "The answer is in the chat" | The opening contradiction: the answer is ready, but **0 of 4 files changed** |
| Deck slide 2: "The professional is the operating system" | The 7 manual steps and the 3 taxes: **context tax · execution gap · review tax** |
| Deck slides 4–5 | Workspace context, native files, assistant + changes, review |
| Strategy `07_PERSONAS.md` | **Maya** (associate, fund finance), **David** (CFO); her pains: copying 100+ numbers, re-cutting after the CFO changes one assumption, `LP_Q3_v11_final_MK.pptx` sprawl, formatting breaking |
| Strategy README | Our wedge: **keeping multi-file packs (Excel → deck → memo) correct**. Single-file AI-in-Office now exists (ChatGPT for Word, Copilot), so we must show the whole pack |
| Real app footage (demo Task 3) | DACH 8.9 → 8.5; memo €71–73m → €74.6m; 10 of 10 changes reviewed and accepted |

## 4. Audience
Fund-finance and portfolio-ops associates, FP&A, bankers and consultants who build recurring board or LP packs. Secondary: AI power users. Feed: LinkedIn, X, YouTube, Instagram.

## 5. Rules
1. **Show the workflow on screen**, at the pace a real person would read it. Every message holds for at least 2.5 s and is large enough to read on a phone.
2. **One task, one number, start to finish:** "DACH Q4 to 8.5 → FY26 €74.6m (was €71–73m)."
3. **The AI's failure must be specific and true to life:** an answer only in chat, files unchanged; a downloaded deck in the wrong template; pasted text with stray `**` markdown; three `_updated(2).pptx` files.
4. **No real AI brand names or logos** ("AI chat", not ChatGPT or Claude). Narration may say "today's chatbots".
5. **Product proof only from real app footage.** Prototype mockups are labelled as such or not used. Never show the internal name "Hermes", file paths, or the failed-step span.
6. **Faces only where they add emotion**: Maya's reactions, not plot. If Dan the AI is used, every Dan beat must be paired with a screen showing exactly what the AI did (Version B).
7. One ending, one line, one CTA.

## 6. Versions we want
| Version | Length | What it is |
|---|---|---|
| **A: "Role Reversal"** (main) | ~75 s, 16:9 | Screen-led truth plus Maya's reactions; narrator |
| **B: "Dan"** | ~75 s | The same story, with the AI played by Dan for comedy; each Dan beat cuts to the screen showing what he actually did |
| **C: Sound-off** | ~75 s | Version A with captions in place of narration (for feeds that autoplay muted) |
| **D: 9:16 short** | ~30 s | The reversal only: "You drive, AI suggests" → "AI drives, you approve" |

## 7. Success test
Show it, with no explanation, to five people from the audience. They should be able to say:
1. "She had to update one number across the model, memo and deck."
2. "The chatbot only told her what to do, so she did it all by hand, and its deck was broken."
3. "Agentic Office did it inside her files and she just approved the changes."
4. They remember the name.
# Research: real, public pain (for SCRIPT_v5)

*Collected 2026-10-12. Quotes are 15 words or fewer; everything else is paraphrased. Reddit and Wall Street Oasis block automated reads, so Reddit-specific threads are not cited; the sources below are the ones that could be opened and checked. "Vendor" = the page sells a fix, so treat its framing with care.*

## A. The AI only talks; the file never changes (execution gap)
1. **Hacker News, ecshafer, 2026-05-15**, https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48151528
   Asked an AI assistant for a slide. It made "an empty powerpoint slide with the default template", told them to download it, then gave separate text "to copy and paste it in".
   → Film: the chat's answer arrives as a download plus text to paste. The human does the assembly.
2. **Hacker News, deckar01, 2026-02-05**, https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46901034
   "It's just a chatbot app… it still doesn't do anything but chat." Asked for a Word document, they got a download link to a template.
   → Film: the chat says "Here's what to change", and the folder shows 0 of 4 files changed.

## B. AI-made decks break the template, the chart and the content
3. **Hacker News, irishcoffee, 2026-04-02**, https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47608376
   Gave an LLM a Word doc and the company PowerPoint template. The deck came back with no text from the source, and six content slides "were identical, and empty."
   → Film: the downloaded deck has the right slide count but the wrong content.
4. **Microsoft Tech Community, "PowerPoint company branding", 2024-02-29**, https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/discussions/microsoft365copilot/powerpoint-company-branding/4072079
   "the templates show in PowerPoint correct… copilot won't seem to utilize them." The poster had "spent tons of time" trying.
   → Film: "template lost" is the most common and most believable failure.
5. **Deckary blog, AI PowerPoint makers tested on a strategy deck, 2026-04-03**, https://deckary.com/blog/ai-powerpoint-presentation-maker *(vendor)*
   The AI "defaulted to generic bar charts and bulleted lists"; the waterfall chart was not met; **35 minutes of reformatting** to fix it.
   → Film: slide 4's chart becomes bullets; a red label reads "chart gone".
6. **MindStudio blog, AI PowerPoint add-in limits, 2026-05-09**, https://www.mindstudio.ai/blog/claude-powerpoint-add-in-limitations-cant-see-slides-hallucination *(vendor)*
   The AI reads a text version of the deck, not the picture, so when asked to update a chart it can "hallucinate those values".
   → Film: the chat's deck shows a number nobody gave it. This motivates the cross-check by hand.
7. **eesel blog, review of AI deck building, 2026-09-21**, https://www.eesel.ai/blog/claude-slides-review *(vendor)*
   The add-in "crashes and fails mid generation, so you need to redo the whole thing"; output is a first draft that needs finishing by hand.
   → Film: "Regenerate" leads to `_updated (1)`, then `_updated (2)`.

## C. Pasting AI text into Word (stray markdown, wrong formatting)
8. **Mac Power Users forum, cwc, 2025-04-13**, https://talk.macpowerusers.com/t/chatgpt-markdown-formatting-issue/40431
   AI text "pastes as plain text with broken formatting" in many apps, and adds stray tabs.
9. **Unmarkdown blog, "Why do asterisks appear when I paste from ChatGPT", 2025–26**, https://unmarkdown.com/blog/why-do-asterisks-appear-when-i-paste-from-chatgpt *(vendor)*
   Paraphrase: the copy button puts raw markdown on the clipboard, and Word has no markdown detection, so `**bold**`, `##` and table pipes `|` arrive as literal characters.
   → Film: the memo paragraph arrives as `**€74.6m**` in the wrong font, and the memo's Table 1 still says €71–73m.

## D. Re-uploading context in every chat (context tax)
10. **OpenAI Developer Community, GPT-4o memory regression thread, July 2025**, https://community.openai.com/t/bug-gpt-4o-memory-regression-context-loss-across-chats-and-inside-threads/1310926
    "Asks to upload the same document every few minutes and forgets what we are doing." (2025-07-09)
    "Every new chat starts from zero" (2025-07-29)
    → Film: a new chat asks her to "upload the files again"; the upload chips crawl a second time.

## E. Version sprawl (final_v7)
11. **Hacker News, many authors, 2025–2026** (Algolia search for "final_final", e.g. https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46318564, https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47993179, https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48409590)
    Real filenames people typed: `v1_final_FINAL_approved_v2.xlsx`, `Dissertation_final_final_v8.docx`, `assessment_framework_draft_v3_final_FINAL.docx`.
    → Film: the Downloads list reads `Board_Deck_Q3_updated.pptx`, `…updated (1).pptx`, `…updated (2).pptx`, `Board Memo Q3 FINAL_v3.docx`. Our own persona file uses `LP_Q3_v11_final_MK.pptx`.

## F. Late-night pack rework in finance
12. **Hacker News, michaelochurch, 2011-11-22**, https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=3263866, and **hncommenter13, 2013-09-13**, https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=6379145 *(older than 2024; kept as background)*
    "proof-reading pitch books at 3:00 am on a Sunday"; memos "largely written between 2 and 5 AM".
13. **IBTimes, 2025**, https://www.ibtimes.com/junior-bankers-spend-hours-building-models-pitchbooks-openai-wants-chatgpt-do-that-work-3807391, and **Financial News via iTiger, 2025**, https://www.itiger.com/hans/news/2495549477
    Paraphrase: banks are hiring ex-bankers to train AI on models and pitchbooks, and planning AI to remove "junior drudge work" such as correcting seniors' mark-ups, after renewed scrutiny of brutal hours.
    → Film: the hour stamps (11:47 PM → 3:12 AM) and David's texts are the believable part, not an exaggeration.
14. **Vault / Street of Walls, IB analyst day-in-the-life** (background), https://streetofwalls.com/articles/investment-banking/learn-the-basics/a-day-in-the-life-of-an-investment-banker/
    Paraphrase: senior comments land after the client meetings end, so revisions run to 1–3 AM; a deck may change every night for two weeks.

## Not found as a public quote (so the film keeps it generic)
- A specific post where a board deck said one number and the memo another. Numbers that don't tie across files are well known in finance (and are in our persona file: "tie-out errors found by LPs"), but I could not open a citable thread. The film uses only our own numbers: €71–73m vs €74.6m.

## The three most usable details
1. **The AI hands you a download and "copy and paste this in"** (HN, 2026). It's the whole "you drive, it suggests" insight in one line.
2. **Template ignored; chart turned into bullets; 35 minutes to fix** (MS forum 2024; Deckary 2026).
3. **"Upload the same document every few minutes"** (OpenAI forum, 2025). It makes the context tax visible.
# Decisions carried forward / release gates

User feedback and team screenshots informed these decisions. Private chat screenshots and phone numbers are intentionally not copied; the useful creative decisions are summarized here.

| Topic | Keep / show | Avoid / still confirm |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Main proposition | Word, Excel, PowerPoint formats in one agentic, collaborative professional workspace | Not just a cross-document trick or generic AI chat; no complete Microsoft 365 replacement promise |
| Hook | Three work cards merge, a little breathing space between app names | No PDF-editing promotion; no rushed list; audience copy says work, not project |
| UI | Actual team-provided screenshot/prototype and new authentic recordings | No generative/repainted controls, invented result, fake clicks, or unsupported UI |
| Prompt to deck | One prompt uses memo + forecast; proposed presentation opens in the main UI | Existing source is prototype; real generation capture and shipping confirmation are required |
| Selective edits | Accept or reject individual proposed changes, without whole-document rewrite | Screenshot proves visible controls, not an accepted/rejected result; capture real action |
| Collaboration | Shared document, presence, changes, proposals | Prototype isn't release proof; confirm actual supported interaction |
| Cross-agent | Context sharing, coordinated handoff, proposed next change; human decides | No guaranteed autonomous completion/sending; confirm and record the actual handoff |
| Time saving | Less copying, less rework, less switching to separate AI chats | No fabricated minutes/percentages or competitive benchmark |
| Local files | Files stored on device; agent works inside workspace; no separate manual upload step | Local storage ≠ local inference. Keep “Cloud AI may process document content.” Product team must confirm exact data flow |
| Privacy tone | Subtle sense of continuity/control through local file tree and user review | No shield/cloud-blocked icon, “privacy solved,” “never uploaded,” “whole files never sent,” or “local-only AI” |
| Art direction | Plain stages, typography, graphics, truthful UI; reuse opening card language | No AI-generated people, photographic office/laptop shots, cluttered unrelated effects |
| Audio | Narration plus jazz-like groove, drum rolls, synchronized SFX | YouTube music rights are unknown. Inherited SFX licenses unresolved; OpenArt subscription isn't clearance |
| Workflow | New request: Claude + OpenArt; keep V11 Remotion baseline for continuity | Do not force earlier Remotion-only preference onto the new requested workflow; do not assume a quality ceiling of any framework |

## Public launch gates

Confirm all advertised features ship. Replace/label prototype sequences honestly. Obtain sanitized product recordings and official logo/CTA. Confirm privacy wording against architecture. Clear final VO/music/SFX/model-output usage rights. Check accessibility/readability and audio/video export. This folder is a production handoff, not a release authorization.
